From f42d20f6399109f2f2b5ec281c584168a2e24f66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:48:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] LU-20603 llapi: add llapi_scan_namespace()

Add llapi_scan_namespace(). It walks a mounted filesystem and gives
the caller one record per object, instead of a formatted line.

The parameter block and the record can grow later:
- lfsp_size says how much of the parameter block the caller knows.
  Bytes past this library's definition must be zero, up to 4096
  bytes. Only whole fields are
  copied, so a size that ends inside a field drops that field.
- lfsp_want says which fields the caller needs, so it pays only for
  those. A bit this library does not know is dropped, not refused,
  and lfsp_got reports what the scan can answer.
- lfsr_valid says which fields were filled. A field the scanner could
  not get has its bit clear, so it is not mistaken for zero.
- An unknown lfsp_flags bit, or reserved bytes that are not zero, are
  refused. Otherwise a newer caller's flag would be ignored silently.

The record starts with a struct statx, so a consumer can cast it to
one and read the Lustre fields after it. Static asserts check the
offset and the size. lfsr_padding names a hole the compiler left.
The prefixes are lfsr_ and lfsp_, because sp_ is already used in the
tree.

Fixes in the shared helpers, so that they can be shared safely:
- The two callers that have no FID clear the record up to lmd_lmm
  before the conversion. lmd_fid held a FID made from the file name,
  stx_mask kept bits from the V1 lmd_st or the name, which could set
  STATX_BTIME with no btime behind it, and lmd_lmmsize is the length
  llapi_get_lum_file_fd() copies by. convert_lmd_statx() clears
  nothing, because cb_find_init() has real values there. This takes
  in LU-20643, which was change 68340.

In the new code: llapi_scan_get_lmv() clears lum_pool_name, so it
never keeps the previous directory's value, and leaves a foreign
directory's LMV alone, since its type is where the MDT index would be
written. STATX_INO is in LLAPI_SCAN_MDT_MASK, because only the ioctl
answers it. LLAPI_SCAN_LMV_FOREIGN asked for alone fetches the LMV.

get_projid() is no longer static, so the gather can use it. Its
per-object messages are now LLAPI_MSG_DEBUG, so a caller can silence
them with llapi_msg_set_level().

llapi_scan_namespace.3 says how long each part of a record stays
valid. Some parts end when the callback returns, and the layout and
LMV buffers stay until the next object is gathered.

lustre/tests/llapi_scan_test.c is new, and sanity test_157c runs it.
Tests 0-9 cover every object once at any thread count, the depth
limit, a consumer stopping the scan, the demand mask, the filter, bad
arguments, the project id, the HSM state and the layout. test10 scans
a tree that is not Lustre: the stat fields are set, and FID, layout,
LMV, MDT index and HSM are clear. It skips itself when the tree is on
Lustre.

Fixes: 11aa7f8704c4 ("LU-11367 som: integrate LSOM with lfs find")
